{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2spuyb5","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"redox-reactions","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"oxidation-and-reduction-reactions","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"preduction-of-the-metal-centre-in-aqueous-permanganate-ion-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-9fld5vwhua9cv1i6","content":"<p>Reduction of the metal centre in aqueous permanganate ion involves</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"3 electrons in neutral medium."},{"identifier":"B","content":"5 electrons in neutral medium."},{"identifier":"C","content":"3 electrons in alkaline medium."},{"identifier":"D","content":"5 electrons in acidic medium."}],"correct_options":["A","C","D"],"explanation":"<p>In an aqueous solution, the reduction of the metal center in permanganate ions (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.69ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.894ex\" height=\"2.554ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -823.8 3047.1 1128.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1051,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msubsup\" transform=\"translate(1651,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(796,411.6) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-305.1) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) varies depending on the me